      "description": "The switch from `??` to `||` inverts the documented behavior: `||` treats every falsy value as absent, so an explicit timeout of 0 is replaced by the 500 default instead of being preserved to disable timing. The removed `??` form already implemented the intended semantics of defaulting only on null/undefined.",
